All 14 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`: validates `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS`, raises HTTP 401 if missing or invalid, returns the username on success.

**`app/database.py`** — Added `allocate_task_id()` with a monotonic counter starting after the last seed task, so newly created tasks get unique IDs.

**`app/main.py`** — Five changes:
- `GET /tasks` — accepts optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters and `page`/`page_size` pagination (defaults: page 1, page_size 20). All filters are combinable.
- `POST /tasks` — requires auth via `require_api_key`, validates `project_id` exists (404 if not), auto-generates ID, returns 201 with the created task.
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth, applies partial updates (`exclude_unset=True` so only sent fields change), preserves others, 404 if not found.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth, removes and returns the task, 404 if not found.
- Added `TaskStatus` and `Depends` imports needed by the new endpoints.
